## Technical Improvements

### 1. Database Layer
**Issues Resolved:**
- Implemented connection pooling with proper limits
- Added parameterized queries preventing SQL injection
- Introduced transaction support for data consistency
- Enhanced error handling with custom error types
- Added environment validation and health checks

### 2. API Security
**Issues Resolved:**
- Implemented environment-based JWT configuration
- Reduced token expiration (15m access, 7d refresh)
- Added token refresh mechanism with session management
- Implemented rate limiting (100 requests/minute per IP)
- Enhanced request tracking with unique IDs

### 3. Type Safety & Validation
**Issues Resolved:**
- Implemented comprehensive input validation
- Added full TypeScript interfaces and proper typing
- Created custom error classes with inheritance
- Added regex-based validation for user inputs
- Implemented business rule validation

### 4. Performance & Scalability
**Issues Resolved:**
- Optimized SQL queries eliminating N+1 problem
- Implemented pagination with metadata
- Added parallel processing with Promise.all
- Reduced memory usage through efficient operations
- Added query performance monitoring

### 5. Code Organization
**Issues Resolved:**
- Implemented separation of concerns (service/data/API layers)
- Applied single responsibility principle
- Eliminated code duplication (DRY principle)
- Standardized error handling across all layers

